msgid "Read object cache in wp-admin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:161
msgid "When disabled, normal wp-admin reads bypass Redis. Writes and invalidations still reach Redis; transients remain readable from Redis when no database mirror is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:162
msgid "Database transient mirror"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:162
msgid "Write transient and site-transient values to both Redis and the database, and read the database on a Redis miss."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:163
msgid "Non-persistent groups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:163
msgid "One exact WordPress cache group per line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:167
#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:1277
msgid "HTML page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:169
msgid "Stores eligible public HTML responses in Redis through advanced-cache.php. No cached pages are written to disk."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:174
msgid "Enable page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:174
msgid "The plugin attempts to add define( 'WP_CACHE', true ); to wp-config.php when needed. If automatic enabling fails, set WP_CACHE to true manually and verify the Status tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:175
msgid "Page TTL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:176
msgid "CDN cache lifetime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:176
msgid "Seconds a CDN or reverse proxy may keep a cache hit, sent as Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=N. Browsers still revalidate every time. Zero disables the header, which is what shared caches see today. Enable this only if you are willing to purge the CDN when content changes, because the CDN does not know about page invalidation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:177
msgid "Clear a page's cache when it is updated"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:177
msgid "Invalidates the updated, published, unpublished, scheduled or deleted post, page or custom post type and all translations detected through WPML or Polylang. Listing pages are handled by the option below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:178
msgid "Clear related taxonomy archives when a post is updated"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:178
msgid "Invalidates archives of current, previous and new assigned terms in public standard and custom taxonomies, including hierarchical parents and terms assigned to WPML or Polylang translations, and the archive of a term that is renamed or deleted. Unrelated taxonomy archives remain cached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:179
msgid "Clear listing pages when content is published"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:179
msgid "When public content is published, changed, unpublished, scheduled or deleted, invalidates the front page, the posts page, post type, author and date archives, search results and cached 404 pages, with all their pagination. Taxonomy archives use the option above when it is enabled, and this one otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:180
msgid "Clear the page cache when the site changes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:180
msgid "Clears the whole HTML page cache after menus, widgets, Customizer settings, the active theme, core site settings, ACF options pages or a plugin, theme or core update change. Deploys that bypass WordPress can run: wp simple-redis-cache purge page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:184
msgid "Clear the whole cache when content changes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:187
msgid "No, clear only what changed (the options above)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:188
msgid "The whole HTML page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:189
msgid "The whole HTML page cache and object cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:191
msgid "Once per request, after a post, page or custom post type is published, updated, unpublished, scheduled or deleted, its categories or tags change, a term is renamed or deleted, or the site changes as described above. Drafts, revisions and autosaves clear nothing. The object cache is cleared as Clear all cache does, transients included, so the pages after a change are slower until the cache fills again. Simplest and always correct, at the cost of a cold cache after every change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:193
msgid "Cache logged-in users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:193
msgid "Disabled is safest. Logged-in variants are isolated by session when enabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:194
msgid "Cache home page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:195
msgid "Cache posts, pages and CPTs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:196
msgid "Cache archives"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:197
msgid "Cache search results"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:197
#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:198
msgid "Kept for at most 10 minutes, in Redis and at a CDN."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:198
msgid "Cache 404 responses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:199
msgid "Cache query strings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:199
msgid "Non-ignored query parameters normally bypass page cache unless this is enabled; supported search parameters are a limited exception. Built-in unsafe parameters always bypass."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:200
msgid "Ignored query parameters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:200
msgid "One exact name or wildcard pattern per line; * and ? are supported. Matching non-sensitive parameters are removed from the cache key; built-in unsafe names cannot be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:201
msgid "Excluded paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:201
msgid "One path pattern per line; * and ? are supported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:202
msgid "Excluded request cookies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:202
msgid "Matching cookies normally bypass page cache. Vary-cookie entries and the default WordPress auth prefixes when logged-in caching is enabled use isolated variants instead. Use one exact name, wildcard pattern, or conventional prefix ending in _ per line. Add every cookie that changes page content, such as a theme's maintenance-mode access cookie, and clear the page cache when such a mode is switched on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:203
msgid "Excluded user agents"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:203
msgid "One case-insensitive substring or wildcard pattern per line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:204
msgid "Cookies that vary the cache key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:204
msgid "One cookie name per line. Useful for language cookies that safely select a page variant. Values must look like a language or locale code (letters, digits, _ and -, up to 32 characters) and, when Polylang, WPML or WP-LOC is active, all name one and the same of its languages; each URL caches at most 16 such variants, and they never get the CDN lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:205
msgid "Allowed response Set-Cookie names"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:205
msgid "Responses setting only these cookie names may be stored; Set-Cookie headers are never replayed from cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:206
msgid "Debug response header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:206
msgid "Send X-Simple-Redis-Cache with HIT, MISS or BYPASS status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:210
#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:1278
msgid "Cloudflare cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:212
msgid "Clears the Cloudflare edge cache alongside this site's own caches. Clearing the origin without clearing the edge leaves visitors on the previous page until the CDN lifetime expires."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:213
msgid "Create a scoped API token in Cloudflare with the Zone / Cache Purge permission limited to this zone. An account-wide Global API Key is not used and is not required."
msgstr ""

