msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:219
msgid "Leave blank to retain the stored token when the option below is checked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:220
msgid "Stored API token"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:221
msgid "Clear Cloudflare with Clear all cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:221
msgid "Purge the whole Cloudflare zone whenever the Clear all cache action runs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:222
msgid "Clear Cloudflare with Clear page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:222
msgid "Purge the whole Cloudflare zone whenever the Clear page cache action runs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:223
msgid "Clear Cloudflare when content is updated"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:223
msgid "Purge the exact URLs this plugin already invalidates on the HTML Page Cache tab, so it requires those options to be enabled. The updated entries, the first page of related term archives and, for listing pages, the home page of each language, the posts page and the post type archive are purged; deeper pagination is not, because Cloudflare purges exact URLs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:224
msgid "Clear the whole Cloudflare zone when content changes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:224
msgid "Purge the whole zone once per request after the same changes as \"Clear the whole cache when content changes\" on the HTML Page Cache tab, and after site changes. It runs once the page cache here has been cleared, so the edge never fetches a stale page back; with the page cache disabled it runs on its own. Replaces the exact-URL purge above, and every page is fetched from the site again afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:247
msgid "The settings were not saved because the submitted section was invalid. Please reload the page and try again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-admin.php:283
msgid "Redis-only object and full-page cache for a single WordPress site. Cache entries use a non-empty WP_CACHE_KEY_SALT when defined, or a generated per-site fallback prefix."
msgstr ""

